description:
When running a mangelhaft test from the IDE a "TimeoutOverflowWarning" is emitted to stderr.

To reproduce:

1. create new N4JS project with package.json:
   ```json
   {
   	"name": "GHOLD_45",
   	"version": "0.0.1",
   	"dependencies": {
   		"org.eclipse.n4js.mangelhaft": "*",
   		"org.eclipse.n4js.mangelhaft.assert": "*"
   	},
   	"n4js": {
   		"projectType": "test",
   		"vendorId": "org.eclipse.n4js",
   		"sources": {
   			"test": [
   				"src"
   			]
   		},
   		"output": "src-gen"
   	}
   }
   ```
2. add an n4js file `A.n4js` as follows:
   ```javascript
   export public class A {
       @Test
       public aTest(): void {
           console.log('A#aTest');
       }
   }
   ```
3. run the test by right-clicking `A.n4js` and selecting "Run As > Test in node.js".

The following output is shown in the console:
```
(node:5142) TimeoutOverflowWarning: 9007199254740991 does not fit into a 32-bit signed integer.
Timeout duration was set to 1.
A#aTest
```

