description:
In Netty 3.5 my created bootstraps with 1 shared Thread-Pool was shutting down just fine. In Netty 3.6 releasing the resources leads to an infinite loop. The following Unit-Test reproduces the error.

```
@Test
public void testRelease() {

    // create bootstraps
    final ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);
    final ClientBootstrap client = new ClientBootstrap(
            new NioClientSocketChannelFactory(pool,
                    Executors.newCachedThreadPool()));
    final ServerBootstrap server = new ServerBootstrap(
            new NioServerSocketChannelFactory(pool,
                    Executors.newCachedThreadPool()));

    // release resources
    System.out.println("Releasing resources - client...");
    client.releaseExternalResources();
    System.out.println("Releasing resources - server...");
    server.releaseExternalResources();
}
```

