description:
This is a copy of github bug #5172. 

In that bug it was stated that my use case ran correctly in 2.1.5 and that the problem was that my client was 2.0.15. We upgraded our code to 2.1.5, but the issue persists. So now I try again in the orient source with my testcase running a fresh distributed 2.1.5 enterprise server, and it fails. 

To reproduce:
Unzip 2 copies of orient enterprise 2.1.5 and make sure they are a setup as a cluster.

Create a new plocal test database and make sure the database is synchronized and distributed over both servers. 

Run the following program in the orient source with tag 2.1.5, I put the class in tests/src/tests/java

```
import com.orientechnologies.orient.core.db.document.ODatabaseDocumentTx;
import com.orientechnologies.orient.core.id.ORID;
import com.orientechnologies.orient.object.db.OObjectDatabaseTx;
import com.orientechnologies.orient.object.metadata.schema.OSchemaProxyObject;

import javax.persistence.Id;
import javax.persistence.OneToOne;
import javax.persistence.Version;
import java.io.Serializable;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

public class OrientTest {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        ODatabaseDocumentTx documentTx = new ODatabaseDocumentTx("remote:localhost/test").open("admin", "admin");

        OObjectDatabaseTx db = new OObjectDatabaseTx(documentTx);

        OSchemaProxyObject schema = db.getMetadata().getSchema();
        db.getEntityManager().registerEntityClass(Parent.class);
        db.getEntityManager().registerEntityClass(Child.class);
        db.getEntityManager().registerEntityClass(OtherThing.class);
        schema.generateSchema(Parent.class);
        schema.generateSchema(Child.class);
        schema.generateSchema(OtherThing.class);
        Parent parent1 = new Parent();
        parent1 = db.save(parent1);

        Parent parent2 = new Parent();
        parent2 = db.save(parent2);


        Child child1 = new Child();
        parent1.getChildren().add(child1);
        parent1 = db.save(parent1);

        Child child2 = new Child();
        parent2.getChildren().add(child2);
        parent2 = db.save(parent2);

        parent1 = db.detachAll(parent1, true);
        parent2 = db.detachAll(parent2, true);


        db.close();

        db.open("admin", "admin");

        db.begin();
        parent1 = db.load((ORID) parent1.getId());
        parent2 = db.load((ORID) parent2.getId());
        Child child3 = new Child();
        OtherThing otherThing = new OtherThing();
        child3.setOtherThing(otherThing);
        otherThing.setRelationToParent1(parent1);
        otherThing.setRelationToParent2(parent2);
        parent1.getChildren().add(child3);
        parent2.getChildren().add(child3);
        db.save(parent1);
        db.save(parent2);
        db.commit();
    }

    public static class Parent {

        @Id
