description:
First, I wanna thank authors on this awesome library! Good job guys!

Okay, right, so I'm using FFmpegFrameRecorder to convert images (BufferedImage) to a video but it seems that duration is incorrect even though frame count is correct. Expected duration is 2 seconds with fps 24 (48 frames total).
I tried passing different options to ffmpeg, no help (like gop, bframe, coder, setpts, preset, movflags, `-r`, etc). Even different containers and different codecs, still the same issue.

Version: JavaCV 1.4.3 and ffmpeg 4.0.2-1.4.3, java 8 and 11

equivalent ffmpeg command `ffmpeg -r 24 -i /tmp/images/%0d.jpg  -pix_fmt yuv420p -c:v libx264  video.mp4` (which works as expected, 24fps, 2 seconds, 48 frames)

a gist of ffprobe output:
```
  Duration: 00:00:01.96, start: 0.000000, bitrate: 39 kb/s
  Stream #0:0(und): Video: h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p, 200x200, 34 kb/s, 24.51 fps, 24 tbr, 12288 tbn, 48 tbc (default)
            "r_frame_rate": "24/1",
            "avg_frame_rate": "1152/47",
            "time_base": "1/12288",
            "nb_frames": "48",
            "nb_read_frames": "48"
```
sample code (you can move `frame` out of the loop to make it run faster, issue will still be reproduced)
```java
import org.bytedeco.javacpp.avutil;
import org.bytedeco.javacv.FFmpegFrameRecorder;
import org.bytedeco.javacv.FFmpegLogCallback;
import org.bytedeco.javacv.FrameConverter;
import org.bytedeco.javacv.Java2DFrameConverter;

import javax.imageio.ImageIO;
import java.awt.image.BufferedImage;
import java.net.URL;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;

import static org.bytedeco.javacpp.avutil.AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P;

public class StreamEncoder {

    static {
        FFmpegLogCallback.set();
        avutil.av_log_set_level(avutil.AV_LOG_TRACE);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Path temp = Files.createTempFile("temp", ".mp4");
        FFmpegFrameRecorder recorder = new FFmpegFrameRecorder(temp.toFile(), 200, 200);
        recorder.setFormat("mp4");
        recorder.setVideoCodecName("libx264");
        recorder.setVideoOption("crf", "23");
        recorder.setPixelFormat(AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P);
        recorder.setFrameRate(24);
        recorder.start();
        try {
            FrameConverter converter = new Java2DFrameConverter();
            for (int i = 0; i < 48; i++) {
                BufferedImage img = ImageIO.read(new URL("https://picsum.photos/200/200/?random"));
                final BufferedImage frame = convertToType(img, BufferedImage.TYPE_3BYTE_BGR);
                recorder.record(converter.convert(frame));
            }
        } finally {
            recorder.close();
        }
        System.out.println("Done");
        System.out.println(temp);
    }

    public static BufferedImage convertToType(BufferedImage sourceImage,
                                              int targetType) {
        BufferedImage image;

        // if the source image is already the target type, return the source image

        if (sourceImage.getType() == targetType)
            image = sourceImage;

            // otherwise create a new image of the target type and draw the new
            // image

        else {
            image = new BufferedImage(sourceImage.getWidth(),
                    sourceImage.getHeight(), targetType);
            image.getGraphics().drawImage(sourceImage, 0, 0, null);
        }

        return image;
    }

}
```

